TDOFDFT Al without a current-dependent potential, evolved to t=0.5 fs.
Use dt=0.001 fs and 501 outputs (initial state plus 500 advances).
The previous dt=0.25 fs trajectory had severe energy drift and amplified
parallel numerical differences. The smaller step is checked against dt/2
and dt/4 at the same physical times; see VALIDATION.md and
../../integrate/validation_tools/check_tdofdft_timestep.py.
The reference is regenerated for the new trajectory; comparison thresholds
are unchanged. This case does not establish exact energy conservation or
the convergence order of the coupled propagator.
